    "body": "A sphere of mass $M$, and radius $R$, is given an initial angular speed, $\\omega_i$ up an inclined plane. The sphere rolls without slipping and comes to rest at a height $h_f$ above its initial position.\n\nWhat is the sphere's \\textbf{angular speed}, $\\omega$ when it reaches a height of $h$ = $\\frac{h_f}{2}$ above its initial position?\n\nNote: Moment of inertia of a sphere is $I = \\frac{2}{5} MR^2$",
